WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.568 --> 00:00:04.036
-Since it's summertime, Tariq
and I had a friendly competition

00:00:04.036 --> 00:00:06.072
to see who could make
the best burger.

00:00:06.072 --> 00:00:08.707
That's right -- it is time
for the first annual --

00:00:08.707 --> 00:00:10.676
is it gonna be annual? --

00:00:10.676 --> 00:00:12.545
"Tonight Show" Burger Off.

00:00:12.545 --> 00:00:15.548
That's right. Now...
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:15.548 --> 00:00:18.051
Right now, we will find out,
finally, once and for all,

00:00:18.051 --> 00:00:19.952
who is the food master.

00:00:19.952 --> 00:00:21.620
The rules are simple.

00:00:21.620 --> 00:00:24.957
We each had to make a burger and
pair it with a side and a drink.

00:00:24.957 --> 00:00:27.259
Whoever makes the
most delicious plate possible

00:00:27.259 --> 00:00:29.662
is the winner
and gets their name engraved on

00:00:29.662 --> 00:00:32.432
"The Tonight Show"
Burger Off Golden Hamburger.

00:00:32.432 --> 00:00:34.467
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:36.268 --> 00:00:39.105
Earlier, Tariq and I
made our burgers,

00:00:39.105 --> 00:00:41.240
and we recorded the whole thing.

00:00:41.240 --> 00:00:42.241
Check it out.

00:00:42.241 --> 00:00:43.843
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:00:46.278 --> 00:00:48.281
-Hey, what's up?
The champ is here.

00:00:48.281 --> 00:00:49.515
I'm Tariq Trotter.

00:00:49.515 --> 00:00:52.618
I'm here to win
probably my third ring.

00:00:52.618 --> 00:00:54.320
♪♪

00:00:54.320 --> 00:00:57.923
I decided to go with
a Kobe beef burger

00:00:57.923 --> 00:01:02.729
on a homemade brioche bun with
garlic-truffle fries.

00:01:02.729 --> 00:01:04.864
I think Jimmy's gonna
try and go high-low.

00:01:04.864 --> 00:01:08.001
There's a place in New York City
that serves a burger

00:01:08.001 --> 00:01:09.936
that's like $1,000 or something.

00:01:09.936 --> 00:01:11.104
There's gold leaf.

00:01:11.104 --> 00:01:13.006
I think he's gonna do
something like that.

00:01:13.006 --> 00:01:14.106
-[ English accent ]
I'm Jimmy Fallon

00:01:14.106 --> 00:01:16.509
and I'm here to make some
[bleep] burgers.

00:01:16.509 --> 00:01:21.014
A champagne double-smashed
mustard burger

00:01:21.014 --> 00:01:23.483
with caviar fries.

00:01:23.483 --> 00:01:26.919
♪♪

00:01:26.919 --> 00:01:29.856
[ Normal voice ] It's a smash
burger that's smashing.

00:01:29.856 --> 00:01:31.123 line:0%
We're going to use this
ground beef right here.

00:01:31.123 --> 00:01:32.124 line:0%
This is chuck.

00:01:32.124 --> 00:01:33.426
This is 70/30.

00:01:33.426 --> 00:01:34.426
Look at this.

00:01:34.426 --> 00:01:37.229
We'll put our meat
into the bottom.

00:01:37.229 --> 00:01:39.498
It shows the exact amount that
you're going to want

00:01:39.498 --> 00:01:41.300
to use for each patty.

00:01:41.300 --> 00:01:43.169
"Jimmy, you're a genius!"

00:01:43.169 --> 00:01:44.703
I already know that.

00:01:44.703 --> 00:01:48.274
This is how I make a hamburger.

00:01:48.274 --> 00:01:51.577
-Kobe beef is something that you
do for a special occasion.

00:01:51.577 --> 00:01:54.580
And this is a special occasion,
in that it's an ass whupping.

00:01:54.580 --> 00:01:56.482
-And you're gonna want to
freshly plop it there

00:01:56.482 --> 00:01:58.751
so that it cooks
in its own juices.

00:01:58.751 --> 00:02:00.520
That's a hot plop.

00:02:01.654 --> 00:02:03.823
-I'm going to put these guys
on the area

00:02:03.823 --> 00:02:06.459
that I've already onioned up.

00:02:06.459 --> 00:02:09.361
I think a mistake that
some people make is that

00:02:09.361 --> 00:02:11.163
they flatten their burgers out.

00:02:11.163 --> 00:02:13.833
-You want to make sure
the burger is smashed so thin.

00:02:13.833 --> 00:02:15.367
You're gonna want it
crispy on that bottom.

00:02:15.367 --> 00:02:18.170
Look at that.
Hello. What's your name?

00:02:18.170 --> 00:02:20.440
Ronald Mc-[bleep]-Donald!

00:02:20.440 --> 00:02:22.408
-A Kobe beef burger will
probably, like,

00:02:22.408 --> 00:02:25.678
have a vegan or
a vegetarian, you know,

00:02:25.678 --> 00:02:28.081
looking both ways
and then taking a little bite,

00:02:28.081 --> 00:02:29.148
take a little nib.

00:02:29.148 --> 00:02:30.349
-Let's get
the champagne poppin'.

00:02:30.349 --> 00:02:31.650
[ Cork pops ]
There you go.

00:02:31.650 --> 00:02:33.552
In this recipe, you're gonna
need some dry mustard,

00:02:33.552 --> 00:02:35.855
1 cup of sugar, three eggs,
and champagne vinegar.

00:02:35.855 --> 00:02:38.357
And you're gonna end up with
this amazing sauce.

00:02:38.357 --> 00:02:40.026
A little champagne-mustard
sauce.

00:02:40.026 --> 00:02:41.461
Mm-hmm.

00:02:41.461 --> 00:02:44.163
I'm just putting it out in the
ether that I'm going to win.

00:02:44.163 --> 00:02:47.300
I make my Loki horns.
Then I go, "Come on.

00:02:47.300 --> 00:02:50.703
I want the Golden Hamburger!

00:02:50.703 --> 00:02:53.739
-What is it?
Ham-- Golden Hamburger Bun?

00:02:53.739 --> 00:02:55.008
Yeah. No, thanks.

00:02:55.008 --> 00:02:57.143
Oh, yeah.
Now we hear that sizzle, too.

00:02:57.143 --> 00:02:59.511
These are homemade fries
that I'm making

00:02:59.511 --> 00:03:01.481
with Yukon gold potatoes,

00:03:01.481 --> 00:03:04.416
using both garlic and truffle,
as well as green onion.

00:03:04.416 --> 00:03:05.918
Those are the fries.

00:03:05.918 --> 00:03:10.256
I went and took, like, a crash
course in making brioche bread,

00:03:10.256 --> 00:03:11.423
and this is the end result.

00:03:11.423 --> 00:03:12.992
-Look, I'm a down-to-earth guy.

00:03:12.992 --> 00:03:14.860
Everyone's like, "Jimmy,
you're a man of the people.

00:03:14.860 --> 00:03:15.862
What do you eat
with your burger?"

00:03:15.862 --> 00:03:17.030
I'm like, "Caviar.

00:03:17.030 --> 00:03:18.330
Pommes soufflé with caviar."

00:03:18.330 --> 00:03:19.665
And look at this
beautiful little crispness.

00:03:19.665 --> 00:03:20.700
Are you watching this?

00:03:21.634 --> 00:03:23.369
Come on.

00:03:23.369 --> 00:03:24.737
Mmm!

00:03:24.737 --> 00:03:28.874
-My drink of choice is going to
be a mescal margarita

00:03:28.874 --> 00:03:32.812
that I'm going to serve in a
hickory-smoked glass.

00:03:32.812 --> 00:03:36.115
Look, I know dope people,
I do dope [bleep]

00:03:36.115 --> 00:03:37.984
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:37.984 --> 00:03:39.551
God damn!

00:03:39.551 --> 00:03:40.787
-Then, of course, your ketchup.

00:03:40.787 --> 00:03:43.556
Then you put it
on your clean plate.

00:03:45.258 --> 00:03:46.659
There you have it.

00:03:46.659 --> 00:03:52.531
Champagne mustard double-smashed
cheeseburger with caviar dreams!

00:03:52.531 --> 00:03:56.035
-Kobe beef burger,
garlic-truffle fries.

00:03:56.035 --> 00:03:57.736
Jimmy, bow down.

00:03:57.736 --> 00:04:00.540
-History could be made.
This is very exciting.

00:04:00.540 --> 00:04:04.176
♪♪
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:04.176 --> 00:04:06.578
[ Both laugh ]

00:04:06.578 --> 00:04:09.048
To decide the winning plate,
we have a special guest

00:04:09.048 --> 00:04:11.450
serving as our
master burger judge.

00:04:11.450 --> 00:04:14.520
He's the author of "The Great
American Burger Book,"

00:04:14.520 --> 00:04:16.055
and "The New York Times"
has called him

00:04:16.055 --> 00:04:18.357
the foremost authority
on hamburgers.

00:04:18.357 --> 00:04:22.795
Please welcome the burger
scholar himself, George Motz!

00:04:22.795 --> 00:04:24.797
♪♪
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:24.797 --> 00:04:26.298
Yes!

00:04:26.298 --> 00:04:28.867
George!

00:04:28.867 --> 00:04:30.103
Thank you for
being here, George.

00:04:30.103 --> 00:04:31.470
I appreciate it.

00:04:31.470 --> 00:04:33.906
How's your summer going?
-It's been great.

00:04:33.906 --> 00:04:34.940
It's all good. Warm.

00:04:34.940 --> 00:04:36.342
-It's about to
get better, George,

00:04:36.342 --> 00:04:39.111
because it's time
to try the burgers.

00:04:39.111 --> 00:04:40.847
Whenever you're ready,
please try

00:04:40.847 --> 00:04:42.548
either burger number 1
or burger number 2.

00:04:42.548 --> 00:04:44.116
It's up to you.
-I'm gonna go in reverse order.

00:04:44.116 --> 00:04:47.419
-Sure, reverse order.
Start with number 2. Go for it.

00:04:47.419 --> 00:04:49.622
-Oh, okay.

00:04:49.622 --> 00:04:51.523
Okay, this is...

00:04:51.523 --> 00:04:54.260
It's -- There's a drink
that goes with this, right?

00:04:54.260 --> 00:04:55.494
-Yeah.

00:04:55.494 --> 00:04:58.664
-It's very smart to get me
buzzed for judging.

00:04:58.664 --> 00:05:00.032
I like that.
-Yeah.

00:05:00.032 --> 00:05:02.135
We're all ways thinking here.

00:05:02.135 --> 00:05:03.769
-Okay, well, hang on a se...

00:05:03.769 --> 00:05:05.337
[ Laughs ]

00:05:05.337 --> 00:05:06.939
-Describe it.
-Where do I go into this thing?

00:05:06.939 --> 00:05:07.940
-Yeah, describe it.
-I see hot peppers.

00:05:07.940 --> 00:05:09.709
-Okay.
-This is big.

00:05:09.709 --> 00:05:13.412
Oh, it's got good --
It has great -- great heft.

00:05:13.412 --> 00:05:14.613
-Ooh, heft!
-Heft is good.

00:05:14.613 --> 00:05:15.815
-You get points for heft, sure.

00:05:15.815 --> 00:05:17.483
-I think I see some jalapeños
in there, too.

00:05:17.483 --> 00:05:19.552
I see ketchup on there, though.
-Mm...

00:05:19.552 --> 00:05:21.988
-Uh-oh.
-Uh-oh.

00:05:21.988 --> 00:05:23.489
-I'm gonna take a bite
'cause I have to,

00:05:23.489 --> 00:05:25.124
but I'm not a big fan of
ketchup on burgers.

00:05:26.625 --> 00:05:28.293
Mmm!

00:05:28.293 --> 00:05:30.563
Mmm!

00:05:30.563 --> 00:05:32.498
That's a tasty burger. Wow!

00:05:32.498 --> 00:05:34.200
-What you are tasting?
-Yes.

00:05:34.200 --> 00:05:36.502
I taste -- oh, jalapeños.
Hot.

00:05:36.502 --> 00:05:39.539
I taste ketchup, unfortunately.
I'm not a big fan of ketchup.

00:05:39.539 --> 00:05:41.708
-Yeah, sorry. Yeah.
-Mmm! I'll get another bite.

00:05:41.708 --> 00:05:42.775
-Yeah.

00:05:42.775 --> 00:05:46.112
-Mmm! It's also on one of
my favorite buns.

00:05:46.112 --> 00:05:49.816
It's a potato roll. I like that.
Mmm!

00:05:49.816 --> 00:05:52.751
Wait. What's on the side here?
Scallops?

00:05:52.751 --> 00:05:56.555
What is that?
Oh, no. It's caviar.

00:05:56.555 --> 00:05:57.957
-You're trying to get me drunk,

00:05:57.957 --> 00:06:01.794
and someone's trying to get me,
obviously, caviar.

00:06:02.528 --> 00:06:04.763
Oh, wow!
That's actually kind of nice.

00:06:04.763 --> 00:06:07.032
-Oh!

00:06:07.032 --> 00:06:09.768
-Chaser.

00:06:09.768 --> 00:06:12.638
-This is interesting.
-Yeah.

00:06:12.638 --> 00:06:15.374
[ Cheers and applause ]
Not a clear winner.

00:06:15.374 --> 00:06:16.442
-It's very good.

00:06:16.442 --> 00:06:18.110
-Not a clear loser either, yeah.

00:06:18.110 --> 00:06:20.246
Okay, that was burger number 2.
Here's burger number 1.

00:06:20.246 --> 00:06:21.247
-Number 1.
-No order.

00:06:21.247 --> 00:06:22.815
-Ooh! Okay.

00:06:22.815 --> 00:06:24.684
Okay.

00:06:24.684 --> 00:06:26.419
There's a a drink --
Oh, I see -- Ah!

00:06:26.419 --> 00:06:28.720
Look at this.
That's a poolside cocktail.

00:06:28.720 --> 00:06:31.290
Ooh! That's a margarita.
I like a margarita.

00:06:31.290 --> 00:06:32.525
That's a champagne, I think?

00:06:32.525 --> 00:06:34.360
-Yeah. I think so.

00:06:34.360 --> 00:06:38.430
-This is -- Not a big fan of the
bun, tell you right now.

00:06:38.430 --> 00:06:40.166
And more ketchup.

00:06:40.933 --> 00:06:43.402
Bun's a little too big. Sorry.
-Well, we tried, you know --

00:06:43.402 --> 00:06:46.505
-It's kind of a --
It's like a throw pillow.

00:06:46.505 --> 00:06:48.407
[ Laughter ]

00:06:48.407 --> 00:06:49.741
And it actually
won't fit in my mouth.

00:06:49.741 --> 00:06:51.477
I have to squeeze it.

00:06:51.477 --> 00:06:52.778
-You have to be
human mouth, yeah.

00:06:52.778 --> 00:06:55.181
-Oh, that's not --
Wow, that's a lot of bread.

00:06:56.516 --> 00:06:58.217
Oh, okay.

00:06:58.217 --> 00:07:00.953
Mm...I get it.

00:07:00.953 --> 00:07:02.688
Is that spice?

00:07:02.688 --> 00:07:04.890
It's some kind of
a ketchup again.

00:07:04.890 --> 00:07:06.692
Okay. Well...

00:07:07.993 --> 00:07:09.028
You guys like ketchup.

00:07:09.028 --> 00:07:10.029
Both of you like
ketchup, obviously.

00:07:10.029 --> 00:07:11.364
-Yeah.

00:07:11.364 --> 00:07:13.699
-Mmm!

00:07:13.699 --> 00:07:15.868
That's fantastic.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:18.670 --> 00:07:23.508
-George, the moment of truth
has come.

00:07:23.508 --> 00:07:26.712
Please write down your choice
for the winning burger --

00:07:26.712 --> 00:07:27.746
okay? -- and put it
into the official

00:07:27.746 --> 00:07:29.982
"Tonight Show" Burger Off
ballot box.

00:07:29.982 --> 00:07:31.450
-Into the box.

00:07:31.450 --> 00:07:33.852
Okay. You lock the box?

00:07:33.852 --> 00:07:35.687
-It's locked there to make sure
it's completely secure.

00:07:35.687 --> 00:07:38.624
Please fasten the ballot
straitjacket.

00:07:38.624 --> 00:07:39.725
-The straitjacket.
I got the straitjacket.

00:07:39.725 --> 00:07:40.760
-We have...

00:07:40.760 --> 00:07:44.263
[ Laughter ]

00:07:44.263 --> 00:07:46.665
Make sure that the vote
is in and secure.

00:07:46.665 --> 00:07:47.767
-There you go.

00:07:47.767 --> 00:07:53.171
-Now, the vote
is securely locked in.

00:07:53.171 --> 00:07:55.507
And, man, I just hope the
kids are watching.

00:07:55.507 --> 00:07:56.908
-Cool. Okay, who won?

00:07:56.908 --> 00:07:58.577
[ Laughter, drumroll ]

00:07:58.577 --> 00:08:00.346
Here we go.
George, please -- Just open it.

00:08:00.346 --> 00:08:02.180
It's not really locked.
-It is locked.

00:08:02.180 --> 00:08:04.417
-No. There you go. Alright.
Let us know.

00:08:04.417 --> 00:08:06.452
The winner is...

00:08:06.452 --> 00:08:07.920
burger number 2!

00:08:07.920 --> 00:08:09.822
-Number 2.
-Yes! That's me!

00:08:09.822 --> 00:08:12.658
[ Dinging ]
♪♪

00:08:12.658 --> 00:08:15.094
Oh, my gosh.

00:08:15.094 --> 00:08:17.997
What?! Oh, my gosh!

00:08:17.997 --> 00:08:19.898
No, please. Are you kidding me?
Oh, my gosh.

00:08:19.898 --> 00:08:22.167
This man knows -- he knows what
he's talking about.

00:08:22.167 --> 00:08:25.337
Mwah! Oh, you guys, I love you!

00:08:25.337 --> 00:08:27.573
[ Cheers and applause ]
I love you! I love you!

00:08:27.573 --> 00:08:30.041
Kids, I love you, kids!
Got to bed.

00:08:30.041 --> 00:08:32.811
-I want to say thanks to
Liv Breads

00:08:32.811 --> 00:08:34.546
in Millburn, New Jersey.

00:08:34.546 --> 00:08:36.649
We couldn't have done this
without you guys.

00:08:36.649 --> 00:08:37.916
-Number one.

00:08:37.916 --> 00:08:39.451
The number-one burger,
right here!

00:08:39.451 --> 00:08:41.687
-Bread Alone, my shop --

00:08:41.687 --> 00:08:43.956
-My thanks to burger scholar
George Motz.

00:08:43.956 --> 00:08:45.124
Stick around.

00:08:45.124 --> 00:08:48.060
We'll be right back with
Emilia Clarke, everybody.

00:08:48.060 --> 00:08:49.562
Oh, my goodness!

00:08:49.562 --> 00:08:51.664
Thank you so much.
I'm a sore winner.

00:08:51.664 --> 00:08:53.666
♪♪
[ Cheers and applause ]

